                <pb facs="0530" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg516"/>

                <head>
                    <seg type="margin">[174]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">*Mr. Davis, Secretary
                        of War, to General Wool, United States
                        Army.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington City</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1854-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi>
                        12, 1854</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In addition to the ordinary duties of the
                    military command to which you have been assigned, it is deemed proper to direct
                    your attention to certain special duties which will devolve upon you. Among
                    these will be the duty of maintaining our international obligations by
                    preventing unlawful expeditions against the territories of foreign powers.</p>
                <p>Confidence is felt that you will, to the utmost of your ability, use all proper
                    means to detect the fitting out of armed expeditions against countries with
                    which the United States are at peace, and will zealously co-operate with the
                    civil authorities in maintaining the neutrality laws.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>JEFFERSON DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                                    War.</hi></item>
                            <item>Brevet Major General <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E.
                                Wool</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">U.S.A.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
